# Source-grounded critique — local biomedical image review workspace

**Disposition:** Keep the proposal’s core architecture and support boundary, with the corrections below incorporated before final. Its most useful claims are already carefully bounded: NGFF gives a common named-axis/scale model but not a general affine; TIFF plane order must come from metadata; the napari label-refresh failure has a real fix-and-test chain; and no cited component proves the 3 GB, recovery, or interoperability targets. The remaining high-risk gaps are the identity model for directory-backed OME-Zarr, mapping canvas positions to stored indices, and exact annotation geometry conventions.

