### Consequential napari chain: wording to retain

Use this precise causal account in the final proposal: the reported Zarr labels were written correctly but the current rendered slice did not refresh; discussion identified that NumPy slices were views while Zarr/TensorStore slices were NumPy copies; the fix explicitly updates the visible slice for non-NumPy-backed data; and the `v0.4.19` test file checks rendered data after paint, fill, and mouse operations across NumPy, Zarr, and TensorStore. The fix commit and tagged test source establish presence of the repair and regression coverage, not that tests ran in this review or that the fix proves a full application’s persistence, performance, or coordinate contract. Keep the source-capture erratum for the patch in force (see C1).

